    "response": "User requested one weighted score for all nine criteria, with preservation carrying 25% and no score ceiling; apply the formula to the selected native reviews and publish the current comparison.",
    "basis": "Pinned native output, executed artifact inventories and complete two-reviewer findings support the selected current round. Immutable candidate browser evidence and desktop/mobile visual review verify the standard comparison and exact test-file viewer.",
    "verdict": "The standard four-model table presents one final /100 score. Nine explicit weighted criteria use the unchanged seven native ratings and separately evidenced preservation and runnable-coverage findings, then average both reviewer totals. Inspect run exposes exact JavaScript test files with Copy and retains every suite reason and source citation. Method is closed initially and discloses four new authors, four reused Minimal artifacts, two fresh blind reviewers, the formula’s adoption after reviews and current-round usage.",
    "criterion": "Do not invent file ratings, reviewer variation or missing evidence. Lost preservation contributes 0 of 25 points; absent runnable coverage contributes 0 of 5 points. Neither limits the other criteria or overrides the whole score. Unresolved required evidence leaves no official score. Preserve all other benchmark data and answers. Backend testing remains excluded from Engineering and Overall.",
